WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE
Scene captions for a silent screen recording of Theia 4.4.4 on Windows.
Written from the recording itself, scene by scene; the times were checked
against its frames. Theia is shown in English; Windows and the browser are
shown in French. The Explorer window, 0:50 to 0:58, is blurred.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.900
Download the setup for your system from the latest release page on GitHub. Here, the Windows x64 setup of 4.4.4.

2
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.900
Open the setup from the Downloads folder.

3
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.900
The setup is one full-screen form in a terminal. It starts with the language, English or French.

4
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.700
Then what this computer is for (all-in-one, server only or player only) and where your films are.

5
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:58.000
The folder is copied from Explorer. The window is blurred in this recording because it shows the maintainer's own files.

6
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.900
It is pasted into the form, which counts the videos in it.

7
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.900
The form shows its plan before anything is written. Then it installs.

8
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.900
Theia is installed. Start it from the Start Menu or the Desktop, or by typing theia in a terminal.

9
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.900
The first time, Windows asks whether the server may use the network. The recording allows it.

10
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.900
Who is watching? Profiles have no password.

11
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.900
Home: the film being shown, and what was added recently.

12
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.900
The films, then the series.

13
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Settings: the general page, with the app language and whether to ask who is watching at startup.
